80-net-setup-link.rules is a symlink to /dev/null, which is the canonical way to
mask one of udev's own rule files.

It disables PREDICTABLE INTERFACE NAMING. Without it eudev renames eth0 to
enp2s0 on the HC-800, and every board.env in the tree names eth0 —
OHC_ID_IFACE, OHC_MDNS_IFACE, OHC_UPLINK_IFACE — so S40net finds nothing and the
box boots perfectly with no network. That is exactly what happened on the first
eudev image: it looked like a hang and was a rename.

Masking rather than renaming the board.env keys, because the kernel name is
stable across this fleet (eth0 on x86, imx6 and davinci alike) while the
"predictable" name encodes the PCI path and would differ per board — which is
the opposite of what the rest of the naming convention is for.
